#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# tree_form

#% text
# `tree_form(x)` shows `x` as a tree: each call's head on a line, its arguments below it, indented. It is a display wrapper: the value is `tree_form(x)` itself, drawn as a tree when shown.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
tree_form(1 + x^2)
#% output
#= add
#= ├─ 1
#= └─ pow
#=    ├─ x
#=    └─ 2

#% cell
tree_form(f(a, g(b, c)))
#% output
#= f
#= ├─ a
#= └─ g
#=    ├─ b
#=    └─ c

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `full_form`, `depth`, `level`
